1
00:02:31,629 --> 00:02:34,149
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece

2
00:02:34,149 --> 00:02:37,109
must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

3
00:02:37,109 --> 00:02:41,749
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

4
00:02:41,749 --> 00:02:44,889
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber

5
00:02:44,889 --> 00:02:46,489
after eating the gum gum fruit,

6
00:02:46,489 --> 00:02:50,229
sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

7
00:02:50,229 --> 00:02:53,229
I'm going to be the king of the pirates!

8
00:02:57,129 --> 00:03:00,609
Two years have passed since the War of the Best in Marine Form.

9
00:03:00,609 --> 00:03:02,869
Reuniting after their special training,

10
00:03:02,869 --> 00:03:05,649
Luffy and his crew continue on to the New World.

11
00:03:05,649 --> 00:03:07,789
Their first stop is Fishman Island,

12
00:03:07,789 --> 00:03:09,649
thousands of feet below sea level,

13
00:03:09,649 --> 00:03:11,889
where they meet King Neptune.

14
00:03:11,889 --> 00:03:16,889
Is to invite you all to the Ryugu Palace!

15
00:03:22,929 --> 00:03:26,669
The Ryugu Palace, taken by the shark that they saved.

16
00:03:30,609 --> 00:03:44,029
A few hours before Luffy met with King Neptune,

17
00:03:44,029 --> 00:03:46,129
something unexpected happened.

18
00:03:46,129 --> 00:03:50,469
An unfortunate encounter with a barrel at Mermaid Cove.

19
00:03:50,469 --> 00:03:53,269
Geez, they sure sealed this thing tight!

20
00:03:53,269 --> 00:03:59,769
There must be something important in there!

21
00:03:59,769 --> 00:04:01,509
Well, let's think.

22
00:04:01,509 --> 00:04:03,889
It's packed up all nice like a treasure chest,

23
00:04:03,889 --> 00:04:05,889
but it's still a barrel, so...

24
00:04:05,889 --> 00:04:07,789
maybe some fancy booze?

25
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:12,129
Oh, come on! Almost there!

26
00:04:12,129 --> 00:04:14,629
That'll be enough! Just give me a second!

27
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:15,689
Ah!

28
00:04:15,689 --> 00:04:20,369
That's right! Stand back!

29
00:04:20,369 --> 00:04:21,869
Thank you very much, ladies!

30
00:04:21,869 --> 00:04:24,369
But I think I can take it from here!

31
00:04:24,369 --> 00:04:27,269
You mean there was a person stuffed in there?

32
00:04:27,269 --> 00:04:28,269
No way!

33
00:04:28,269 --> 00:04:49,949
I'm free!

34
00:04:49,949 --> 00:04:54,729
Thank you so much for your help!

35
00:04:54,729 --> 00:04:57,029
I truly couldn't have done it without you!

36
00:04:57,029 --> 00:05:00,729
There's no need to run away!

37
00:05:00,729 --> 00:05:02,529
Hurry! Get to the water!

38
00:05:02,529 --> 00:05:03,529
Ah!

39
00:05:03,529 --> 00:05:04,529
Ah!

40
00:05:04,529 --> 00:05:05,529
Ah!

41
00:05:05,529 --> 00:05:06,529
Ah!

42
00:05:06,529 --> 00:05:07,529
Ah!

43
00:05:07,529 --> 00:05:08,949
Too bad! Too slow!

44
00:05:08,949 --> 00:05:09,949
Ah!

45
00:05:09,949 --> 00:05:10,949
Ah!

46
00:05:10,949 --> 00:05:11,949
Whoa!

47
00:05:11,949 --> 00:05:15,949
What is this?

48
00:05:15,949 --> 00:05:16,949
I'm sinking!

49
00:05:16,949 --> 00:05:17,949
It's mud!

50
00:05:17,949 --> 00:05:19,289
But where did it all come from?

51
00:05:19,289 --> 00:05:20,849
How very observant of you,

52
00:05:20,849 --> 00:05:23,049
though it's more like quicksand, technically.

53
00:05:23,049 --> 00:05:25,349
Consider it my own personal swarm!

54
00:05:25,349 --> 00:05:28,549
This is the power of the Swamp Swamp Fruit!

55
00:05:28,549 --> 00:05:30,849
Hardly glamorous, but I don't mind!

56
00:05:30,849 --> 00:05:33,849
Oh, and by the way, I wouldn't struggle if I were you!

57
00:05:33,849 --> 00:05:34,849
Ah!

58
00:05:34,849 --> 00:05:35,849
No!

59
00:05:35,849 --> 00:05:38,349
It only makes you sink faster!

60
00:05:38,349 --> 00:05:39,549
Someone help!

61
00:05:39,549 --> 00:05:41,049
Oh, stop screaming!

62
00:05:41,049 --> 00:05:42,549
I'm not gonna kill you!

63
00:05:42,549 --> 00:05:45,049
I'll just suck you into a mucky hellhole!

64
00:05:45,049 --> 00:05:46,229
Help me!

65
00:05:46,229 --> 00:05:46,729
What?

66
00:05:46,729 --> 00:05:48,269
Are you brain-dead, lady?

67
00:05:48,269 --> 00:05:50,469
I said stop screaming, didn't I?

68
00:05:50,469 --> 00:05:51,969
Just give it up already!

69
00:05:51,969 --> 00:05:52,969
Initially!

70
00:05:52,969 --> 00:05:54,469
You're fine!

71
00:05:54,469 --> 00:05:57,469
Calm down and take a nap, why don't you?

72
00:05:57,469 --> 00:05:58,469
Hee hee!

73
00:05:58,469 --> 00:05:59,469
Hee hee!

74
00:05:59,469 --> 00:06:00,469
Hee hee!

75
00:06:00,469 --> 00:06:01,469
Hee hee hee!

76
00:06:01,469 --> 00:06:02,469
Hee hee hee hee!

77
00:06:02,469 --> 00:06:03,469
Hee hee hee hee!

78
00:06:03,469 --> 00:06:04,469
Hee hee hee hee!

79
00:06:04,469 --> 00:06:05,469
Hee hee hee hee!

80
00:06:05,469 --> 00:06:06,469
Hee hee hee hee!

81
00:06:06,469 --> 00:06:10,469
Hee hee hee hee!

82
00:06:10,469 --> 00:06:14,469
Hee hee hee hee!

83
00:06:14,469 --> 00:06:16,469
It's a good thing my body's a bottomless pit,

84
00:06:16,469 --> 00:06:18,469
since there's plenty more treasure to put in it!

85
00:06:18,469 --> 00:06:19,469
Huh.

86
00:06:19,469 --> 00:06:22,469
Let me think here, how much do mermaids sell for?

87
00:06:22,469 --> 00:06:25,469
Seventy million at auction, right?

88
00:06:25,469 --> 00:06:27,469
And I nabbed three of them!

89
00:06:27,469 --> 00:06:29,469
That is quite the catch, I must say!

90
00:06:29,469 --> 00:06:31,469
Hee hee hee hee hee!

91
00:06:31,469 --> 00:06:34,469
Those stupid straw hats help me out after all!

92
00:06:34,469 --> 00:06:36,469
If it gets me a free pass through immigration,

93
00:06:36,469 --> 00:06:38,469
you can lock me in a barrel any time!

94
00:06:38,469 --> 00:06:41,469
So what if my plan to cash in on their bounties

95
00:06:41,469 --> 00:06:42,469
didn't quite pan out?

96
00:06:42,469 --> 00:06:44,469
Now I can steal all the mermaids I want!

97
00:06:44,469 --> 00:06:47,469
Hee hee hee hee hee hee hee!

98
00:06:47,469 --> 00:06:48,469
Hmm.

99
00:06:49,469 --> 00:06:50,469
Isshili!

100
00:06:50,469 --> 00:06:52,469
Where'd she run off to?

101
00:06:52,469 --> 00:06:55,469
I'm sure I heard her call for help.

102
00:06:55,469 --> 00:06:56,469
Oh, Isshili!

103
00:06:56,469 --> 00:07:00,469
Back in the present.

104
00:07:00,469 --> 00:07:02,469
In the Port Town of Coral Hill.

105
00:07:02,469 --> 00:07:05,469
Located in the Ryuugu Kingdom.

106
00:07:05,469 --> 00:07:08,469
The Straw Hat Pirates!

107
00:07:08,469 --> 00:07:11,469
They must be the ones who kidnapped your friends from Mermaid Cove!

108
00:07:11,469 --> 00:07:12,469
Who else could it have been?

109
00:07:12,469 --> 00:07:13,469
Hold on.

110
00:07:13,469 --> 00:07:15,469
They saved Kaimi from kidnappers!

111
00:07:15,889 --> 00:07:17,349
I'm sure you must be mistaken.

112
00:07:17,649 --> 00:07:20,109
They were nice. They aren't here to cause any trouble.

113
00:07:20,669 --> 00:07:22,089
Maybe they needed a hostage.

114
00:07:22,529 --> 00:07:23,169
But why?

115
00:07:23,429 --> 00:07:25,029
First off, let's look at the facts.

116
00:07:25,309 --> 00:07:29,169
Excluding us guards and you mermaids, there was nobody else at the cove around that time.

117
00:07:29,829 --> 00:07:32,329
And those thugs from the Fishman District were forced to flee.

118
00:07:32,829 --> 00:07:36,569
A number of the Straw Hats left, but a portion of the crew is still unaccounted for.

119
00:07:36,569 --> 00:07:38,789
We don't know what their intentions may be.

120
00:07:40,069 --> 00:07:43,289
The temptation for humans to kidnap mermaids is just too great.

121
00:07:43,289 --> 00:07:48,069
They're traded at a high price all over the world and we have criminals like them to thank.

122
00:07:48,209 --> 00:07:51,309
But they weren't just any pirates. They saved Kami from slavery.

123
00:07:51,629 --> 00:07:53,629
Pirates often make friends with mermaids.

124
00:07:53,889 --> 00:07:57,929
And then when they come down here, they use that relationship to kidnap them.

125
00:08:00,569 --> 00:08:01,749
Prince Fukuboshi!

126
00:08:02,169 --> 00:08:05,609
Are you certain, Madam Charlie, this vision that you saw?

127
00:08:06,029 --> 00:08:09,149
It is of dire importance, so I must be sure of its accuracy.

128
00:08:10,429 --> 00:08:12,389
Your silence speaks volumes.

129
00:08:12,389 --> 00:08:16,629
Then it is as you say, Straw Hat will bring ruin to this island.

130
00:08:17,909 --> 00:08:20,569
Here, Madam Charlie. I brought you some water.

131
00:08:25,809 --> 00:08:30,969
It's true. I saw it all loud and clear. Such an awful future.

132
00:08:31,369 --> 00:08:33,729
The accuracy of your predictions is well known.

133
00:08:33,969 --> 00:08:37,169
I'm convinced that we must approach this matter with the utmost caution.

134
00:08:37,169 --> 00:08:39,589
It is quite the shame, though.

135
00:08:40,269 --> 00:08:45,969
They seem to have a good reputation with the mermaids, and they saved my sister's pets, so I wanted to treat them kindly.

136
00:08:46,449 --> 00:08:51,129
But now that this new development has come to light, I fear that I must keep a close eye on them.

137
00:08:51,949 --> 00:08:54,449
We have no choice but to take them all into custody.

138
00:08:54,449 --> 00:09:00,989
Around the same time, nearby in the high-class district known as Fishfilly Hills.

139
00:09:01,729 --> 00:09:02,569
They're gone.

140
00:09:03,289 --> 00:09:05,369
Those weren't just ordinary pirates, were they?

141
00:09:05,949 --> 00:09:10,509
Otherwise, King Neptune wouldn't have given them a personal invitation to Ryugu Palace, huh?

142
00:09:10,509 --> 00:09:16,129
Careful you don't fall.

143
00:09:17,029 --> 00:09:18,349
Neptune!

144
00:09:20,829 --> 00:09:21,429
Whoooo!

145
00:09:22,749 --> 00:09:24,169
Ja, ja!

146
00:09:24,729 --> 00:09:32,109
Ja, mon. Ja, mon. Ja, mon. Ja, mon. Ja, mon. Ja, mon. Ja, mon. Ja, mon.

147
00:09:32,789 --> 00:09:34,469
Neptune!

148
00:09:34,469 --> 00:09:36,469
Neptune!

149
00:09:36,469 --> 00:09:37,589
Neptune!

150
00:09:51,349 --> 00:09:53,349
Qu simplicity!

151
00:09:54,609 --> 00:09:55,689
I don't get it...

152
00:09:55,689 --> 00:09:56,789
What's Jamon?!

153
00:09:57,269 --> 00:09:58,689
Sounds dumb to me!

154
00:09:58,689 --> 00:09:59,329
Ahahaha!

155
00:10:01,489 --> 00:10:03,489
God, are you stupid or just playing crazy?!

156
00:10:03,889 --> 00:10:05,389
You got invited to the royal palace!

157
00:10:05,389 --> 00:10:06,489
DON'T BE A PUNK!

158
00:10:06,989 --> 00:10:08,389
Ha ha ha!

159
00:10:08,889 --> 00:10:11,989
You have no idea how much my daughter loves that shark.

160
00:10:12,089 --> 00:10:13,489
It's her favorite pet.

161
00:10:14,189 --> 00:10:15,189
Mmm.

162
00:10:15,889 --> 00:10:17,889
Megalo's never coming back, she said.

163
00:10:18,189 --> 00:10:19,889
Tears welling up in her eyes.

164
00:10:20,189 --> 00:10:22,889
I had no idea that he'd been attacked by the Kraken.

165
00:10:23,189 --> 00:10:26,289
You have my gratitude for rescuing him from danger.

166
00:10:26,389 --> 00:10:27,689
Cha-cha!

167
00:10:28,589 --> 00:10:31,889
I can't really take credit, but whatever.

168
00:10:31,889 --> 00:10:32,589
It all worked out.

169
00:10:32,589 --> 00:10:34,889
So the princess has a shark for a pet, huh?

170
00:10:34,889 --> 00:10:36,589
Oh, what's that, Papagu?

171
00:10:36,689 --> 00:10:40,189
Could it be that you're not as intimate with the princess as you claim?

172
00:10:43,089 --> 00:10:45,089
It did sound fishy.

173
00:10:46,389 --> 00:10:49,389
Aquatic puns aside, I feel so bad for Sanji.

174
00:10:50,589 --> 00:10:51,689
He's stuck in bed,

175
00:10:52,089 --> 00:10:55,089
and he wanted to see the mermaid princess more than anyone else.

176
00:10:55,389 --> 00:10:58,689
He's had a lot of bad luck lately, and it hasn't even been his fault.

177
00:10:59,189 --> 00:10:59,889
Mostly.

178
00:10:59,889 --> 00:11:06,189
But if she's got a pet shark, she might be kind of intense.

179
00:11:06,689 --> 00:11:08,089
Are you sure this is okay?

180
00:11:10,089 --> 00:11:13,089
I mean, someone like me going to Ryugu Palace.

181
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:17,389
He said we could bring our friends, and you guys definitely make the cut.

182
00:11:17,889 --> 00:11:19,389
This is a rare opportunity.

183
00:11:19,389 --> 00:11:20,389
Just enjoy it.

184
00:11:20,789 --> 00:11:23,289
And if you think it's bad, enjoy it even more.

185
00:11:23,289 --> 00:11:25,289
Ha-ha-ha.

186
00:11:25,389 --> 00:11:30,089
By the way, I sent my sons to fetch you, but they took too long and I grew impatient.

187
00:11:30,089 --> 00:11:32,089
I hope they returned in the meantime.

188
00:11:32,889 --> 00:11:38,289
We're holding a banquet, you see, and I simply can't stand to wait on any more guests.

189
00:11:38,589 --> 00:11:40,589
I think we're going to get along great.

190
00:11:40,989 --> 00:11:42,589
Crew, stop drooling!

191
00:11:42,889 --> 00:11:46,989
Oh, speaking of guests, I already invited one of your crewmates.

192
00:11:47,189 --> 00:11:48,489
He's at the palace now.

193
00:11:48,589 --> 00:11:48,889
Huh?

194
00:11:49,589 --> 00:11:52,189
I must say he was a bit lacking in manners, though.

195
00:11:52,389 --> 00:11:58,389
He started drinking before the banquet and wouldn't listen to reason when I advised him to wait for the other guests to arrive.

196
00:11:58,389 --> 00:12:00,889
I seem to have forgotten his name.

197
00:12:01,089 --> 00:12:02,389
Gotta be Zoro.

198
00:12:02,889 --> 00:12:03,889
That's Zoro.

199
00:12:04,389 --> 00:12:05,389
Zori!

200
00:12:05,889 --> 00:12:06,889
It's Zoro, okay?

201
00:12:06,889 --> 00:12:07,889
Zoro!

202
00:12:10,889 --> 00:12:11,889
Don't worry.

203
00:12:12,389 --> 00:12:18,389
As surely as they found him, my soldiers will find the rest of your crew and bring them to the palace.

204
00:12:18,889 --> 00:12:21,889
Hey, got any idea where everyone else went, Nami?

205
00:12:22,389 --> 00:12:23,389
Oh, uh...

206
00:12:23,389 --> 00:12:28,389
Oh, so many cool shops down here!

207
00:12:28,889 --> 00:12:29,889
Not to mention plenty of people.

208
00:12:30,389 --> 00:12:33,389
If we ask around enough, I'm sure somebody will have the info we're looking for.

209
00:12:33,889 --> 00:12:35,889
Oh, yeah? Then do you want to handle it?

210
00:12:35,889 --> 00:12:37,889
If you're looking to shop, that's fine.

211
00:12:37,889 --> 00:12:40,389
But I've got an errand of my own I'd like to take care of.

212
00:12:41,389 --> 00:12:43,889
This is where my old shipwright master came from.

213
00:12:43,889 --> 00:12:53,389
If his family is still down here, I want him to know what an inspiration he was, and that he was a true man to the bitter end.

214
00:12:54,889 --> 00:12:59,389
I know we just got back together, but if you don't mind, I'd like to do this on my own.

215
00:12:59,889 --> 00:13:01,889
It sounds like it's pretty important, so sure.

216
00:13:02,389 --> 00:13:04,389
There's something I'd like to see while we're here, too.

217
00:13:04,389 --> 00:13:05,889
Oh, okay.

218
00:13:05,889 --> 00:13:10,389
It's not often that I get to explore a culture that's completely removed from the surface world.

219
00:13:10,889 --> 00:13:16,389
Someone with a discerning eye may uncover its secrets, or even some pieces of a forgotten history.

220
00:13:16,889 --> 00:13:18,389
That's a Robin thing.

221
00:13:18,889 --> 00:13:19,389
For sure.

222
00:13:20,889 --> 00:13:23,389
So we split up again, but it wasn't a big deal.

223
00:13:23,889 --> 00:13:25,389
No trouble on your end, right?

224
00:13:25,889 --> 00:13:28,389
Uh, well, maybe an itty-bitty bit.

225
00:13:28,389 --> 00:13:33,889
Hey, Fish King, I have a question.

226
00:13:34,389 --> 00:13:38,389
That's not Neptune the god of the sea to you!

227
00:13:42,889 --> 00:13:48,389
If we're 10,000 meters below sea level, why is it so bright and sunny everywhere we go?

228
00:13:48,889 --> 00:13:53,889
Well, that's likely what our ancestors thought when they first arrived here.

229
00:13:53,889 --> 00:13:57,889
This is the only place in the deep sea that light reaches.

230
00:13:58,389 --> 00:14:04,389
It is a glorious, glowing beacon for all of fish mankind, and has been for as long as anyone can remember.

231
00:14:04,889 --> 00:14:13,389
We owe it all to the giant Suntree Eve, whose mighty roots stretch to these depths, carrying shimmering sunlight along with them.

232
00:14:13,889 --> 00:14:14,889
Suntree?

233
00:14:15,389 --> 00:14:19,889
So are its roots bioluminescent, or does it just transfer sunlight from the surface?

234
00:14:19,889 --> 00:14:24,889
The latter, it seems, though scientists have puzzled over the specifics for ages.

235
00:14:25,389 --> 00:14:29,889
The respiration of its roots also supplies oxygen from the surface to our island.

236
00:14:30,389 --> 00:14:34,889
Regardless, we owe our entire civilization to this single mystic tree.

237
00:14:35,389 --> 00:14:39,889
So it's like the big brother, or in this case, big sister, of the mangroves in Sabaody.

238
00:14:40,389 --> 00:14:42,889
Hey, hairy fish dude, I'm getting hungry!

239
00:14:43,389 --> 00:14:43,889
Come on!

240
00:14:45,389 --> 00:14:47,389
We'll be there soon.

241
00:14:47,389 --> 00:14:48,389
We'll be there soon.

242
00:14:51,389 --> 00:14:53,889
It's huge!

243
00:14:54,389 --> 00:14:55,889
That's the entrance.

244
00:14:56,389 --> 00:14:56,889
Get ready.

245
00:14:57,889 --> 00:14:58,889
Ha ha ha!

246
00:14:58,889 --> 00:14:59,389
Ding dong.

247
00:14:59,389 --> 00:14:59,889
Yeah?

248
00:14:59,889 --> 00:15:00,389
Neptune.

249
00:15:00,389 --> 00:15:00,889
Oh!

250
00:15:00,889 --> 00:15:01,389
Hello, your highness!

251
00:15:01,389 --> 00:15:02,389
Allow me to open the gate!

252
00:15:02,389 --> 00:15:03,389
Here.

253
00:15:03,389 --> 00:15:04,389
You'll want one of these.

254
00:15:04,389 --> 00:15:05,389
Oh!

255
00:15:05,389 --> 00:15:06,389
Oh!

256
00:15:06,389 --> 00:15:07,389
Oh!

257
00:15:07,389 --> 00:15:08,389
Oh!

258
00:15:08,389 --> 00:15:09,389
